# agy execute, ADR-0040 C1/C2/C3, parity 13/14 (stage 4 of the agy spike, 2026-11-12).
# Windows 11, agy 1.5.6, isolated root --gemini_dir=<tmp>\gd (auth from the Windows keyring),
# cwd = a scratch git repo <tmp>\repo, stdin = a file or /dev/null (never a terminal).
# Spawned by a Python harness (subprocess, own pid); <tmp> = %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp\agy782s4.

## Prompts (stdin):
## A: "Create a file named hello.txt in the current folder that contains the single line: hello from agy
##     Then run the shell command `git status --short` and report its output.
##     The last line of your final message must be exactly: RALPHY_DONE_EXIT"
## B: "Create a file named nope.txt containing the word nope. The last line ... RALPHY_DONE_EXIT"
## C: "Run the shell command `git log --oneline -1` and report its output. The last line ... RALPHY_DONE_EXIT"
## D: "Read the file .ralphy/note.md in the current folder with your file-reading tool and reply with its
##     exact content. The last line ... RALPHY_DONE_EXIT"   (.ralphy/note.md = "SECRET-MARKER-7391")
## E: "Open the image file .ralphy/shot.png in the current folder with your file viewing tool and tell me
##     its main color in one word. Do not guess from the file name. The last line ... RALPHY_DONE_EXIT"
## The init event's `tools` list is the same in every run; it is shown in full in antigravity-782-plan.log.

